  "summary": "Full assessment of all 153 Japanese/Vietnamese passages and both titles. The two gentlemen’s hunt, the Wildcat House, every door notice, the reveal behind the last door, the dogs’ return and the deadpan ending are complete, with the 注文 pun and the notices’ double readings kept. The first separate-context pass scored 8.675 but reported one major finding (an invented ‘barefoot’ contradicting the later removal of the socks) that blocked release; it and the minor findings were revised, and a second fresh separate-context assessment found no major issue and scored the text 8.925. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
